 ],
 "literal": "When told, will be of use the noble; sugarcane-like, when crushed, will be of use the base.",
 "translation": "The noble will be of help as soon as they are told of a need. The base, like sugarcane, will yield their benefit only when crushed.",
 "modern": "சான்றோர்கள் ஒரு குறையைச் சொன்னவுடனேயே உதவி செய்வார்கள். ஆனால் கயவர்கள், கரும்பைப் போல நசுக்கிப் பிழிந்தால்தான் மற்றவர்களுக்குப் பயன்படுவார்கள்.",
 "explanation": "This couplet contrasts how noble and base people offer help. The word 'சொல்ல' indicates that noble people readily provide assistance the moment a need is spoken. In contrast, base people are compared to sugarcane. Just as sugarcane yields its sweet juice only when it is physically crushed ('கொல்ல'), base people will only be of use when they are forced or pressured.",
